why does mark harmon have a reduced role  in season 19 of ncis and what do his  cast mates really think of him ncis the  cbs police procedural drama is currently  in the middle of airing its 19th season  having first aired in 2003 the popular  series is nearing two full decades on  the air which is an impressive feat for  just about any television show created  by donald p belisario and don mcgill  ncis follows the major case response  team special agents of the naval  criminal investigative service in  washington dc for much of the show's run  the fictional team was led by  supervisory special agent leroy jethro  gibbs played by mark harmon who is  widely considered the face of the show  however in october 2021 the hollywood  reporter wrote that harmon would no  longer be working on the show as a  series regular with season 19 episode 4  acting as a conclusion to gibb's story  for now executive producer and  showrunner steven d binder said in a  statement as an executive producer and  dear friend mark continues to be an  integral part of the fabric of the show  so regarding the future of gibbs as long  time fans of the show may have noticed  over the years never count leroy jethro  gibbs out still harmon has exited the  series at least for the time being  leaving fans to reflect on his legacy  luckily for us tv insider gathered up  comments made about harmon by his ncis  co-stars in which they reveal what it  was like to work with him on the set of  the show naturally they all have good  things to say to start with david  mccallum who plays dr donald ducky  mallard credited harman with creating a  productive working environment mccallum  said in 2007 there was always a certain  degree of chaos at one point during the  series production but it's all gone now  mark was instrumental in putting our  house in order i really thank him for  that in 2009 co-star michael weatherly  who played senior field agent anthony  denozzo through season 13 complimented  harmon's onset behavior saying harman is  a very rare person in this business  because there's no assistant no  entourage mark is largely just a very  straightforward approachable calm  assertive guy he's not a people pleaser  in 2019 cody di pablo who joined in  season three as special agent zeva david  said of harmon we were always trying to  infuse scenes with different things try  something new mark has been here for  years and he's still bringing it even  those closest to harman recognized his  impressive professionalism harmon's  real-life wife paul dauber who played  marcy warren in later seasons raved  about harmon in 2021 saying mark is for  the best of everybody and everything his  ego does not extend he just wants it all  to work  we'll definitely all miss harmon's  on-screen presence in ncis just as his  co-stars will miss him both on and off  the screen being that leroy jethro gibbs  was the head of ncis major case response  team mark harmon was considered the lead  of the show as the lead actor on the  series harmon's role came with different  responsibilities than the other roles in  the cast sean murray who plays tim mcgee  told country living that mark harmon was  number one and explained we wouldn't be  here 16 years later if it wasn't for  harmon harmon is a very special  individual during an interview with  build cody dipoblo also revealed that  harmon was one of her mentors you know  he's a friend mentor you know he's uh  um he was always like a father figure to  me  referencing their characters she  explained obviously zeva and gibbs have  that but cody and mark have that as well  when it came to being the lead actor  michael weatherly relied on harmon's  advice when he got his own series lead  role on the cbs drama bull weatherly  told usa today it's been very  illuminating and given me a great deal  of insight and regard for what mark  harmon was doing all those years on ncis  when i was like how come he doesn't have  as much fun as the rest of us it's clear  that harman remains beloved by viewers  and cast members alike check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  tv shows are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

